Test tooling and fixtures only; no product files.

F1: the module.ver parser is a reimplementation (not a vendored copy) of
the small create_rc.parse_module_ver loop, with an MPL 2.0 header. It
FAILs on any % directive other than %define/%include, and on an
undefined @X@ in a company or copyright value.

F2: before invoking makensis, refuse an include set that contains
!system, !execute, !appendfile, !delfile, !makensis, !packhdr,
!finalize, !uninstfinalize, !getdllversion, or !gettlbversion. Fixtures
for !system and !appendfile target sentinel paths; they are refused and
write nothing.

F3: refuse !if / !ifdef / !ifndef in branding.nsi. The wrapper starts
with Unicode true. makensis is taken from $MAKENSISU, then
~/.mozbuild/nsis/bin/makensis, then PATH as a labelled fallback. The
binary, version, and source are recorded. This is not a full
build-environment mirror.

F4: company and publisher values must be printable ASCII after
resolution. The wrong п→n lookalike map entry is removed.

All earlier fixtures still fail; the real tree still passes.

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
